436
00:48:27.190 --> 00:48:42.479
Michi Rossmeier: Yeah, so what I… I mean, the only downside of using foot straps, especially in the beginning, is that you can get stuck when, you know, when you have this… the thing where the foil… the foil… big foils, they fall, and when they fall, I mean, every foil

437
00:48:42.590 --> 00:48:45.289
Michi Rossmeier: If you misbalance, it can fall.

438
00:48:45.320 --> 00:49:01.379
Michi Rossmeier: The small foils, you can get them back. You can correct them, usually, more or less easily, but a big foil, once it falls over a certain point, it will just fall, and if you're not aware of that in that moment, then you can be stuck in a footstrap, and it can

439
00:49:01.380 --> 00:49:08.810
Michi Rossmeier: Gil Preuss, hurt your foot. And many have done that, for sure, and that's why many teachers, they… of course, they don't want to risk that.

440
00:49:08.870 --> 00:49:17.959
Michi Rossmeier: So they go without… just don't put footstraps, and then you would just fall off. And even if you fall in the direction of the fall, usually somehow you miss it.

441
00:49:18.160 --> 00:49:37.470
